{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Train Of Thought feels like a natural next choice after 10.000 Days because I want heaviness with intricate arrangements; Saturday Night Wrist also appeals through its atmosphere and layers.",
    "Us and Them and Someone In Control fit my interest in melodic, direct heavy rock, while The Oncoming Storm connects with the aggressive riffs I enjoy in Advance And Vanquish and In Flames."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger shares the heaviness of albums I have explored, but its raw, abrasive sound lacks the melodic hooks and layered heaviness I want today.",
    "Glorious Burden interests me less because its theatrical approach is not my current preference. Falling Away leaves me uncertain because I cannot confidently identify the album or connect it to what I want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to assume that enjoying heavy music means I want any kind of heaviness, when texture, melody, and arrangement strongly affect my interest.",
    "My interest in metal seems to carry too much weight when an album's theatrical character makes it a weaker match for my mood."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interest in 10.000 Days makes heavy progressive music with atmosphere and intricate arrangements especially appealing right now.",
    "Melodic hooks matter across both my hard rock and heavier listening. An album can fit those interests broadly without being something I would prioritize today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in heavy rock and metal, but only some capture the melody, atmosphere, and intricate arrangements I want right now."
}"}
